This licence covers the files in the enterprise/ directory of the Qualor repository and the
compiled form of them that ships in the qualor/server image at /app/enterprise ("the Software").
Everything outside enterprise/ is licensed under the MIT licence in the root LICENSE file.

1. Source-available, not open source. You may read the Software, and copy and modify it for
   development and testing, without a subscription.

2. Copies that are not in use. Every copy of Qualor carries the Software, and the Qualor server
   loads it only while a licence key is configured. While no licence key is configured and the
   server does not load the Software, possessing it, running Qualor, building Qualor from
   unmodified source, and mirroring or redistributing the unmodified Software is not use of the
   Software under this licence and needs no subscription.

3. Production use. You may use the Software in production only if you (and any organisation you
   act for) have a valid, paid Qualor Enterprise subscription, evidenced by a licence key issued
   for you, and you comply with the subscription terms. "Production" means any use other than
   development and testing. Production use is limited to what that key enables:
   a. the features the key lists;
   b. the period in which the key is valid, including the 14-day grace period after it expires,
      during which the server keeps the licensed features on. After the grace period the server
      turns them off, and production use of the Software ends until a valid key is configured.

4. Modifications. You may make and publish patches to the Software. Modified versions may be used
   in production only under a valid subscription, as in section 3.

5. The licence key. You may not remove, disable, bypass or circumvent the licence-key check or
   the limits it enforces (section 3), or make the licensed features available to anyone without
   a subscription.

6. Redistribution. You may redistribute the Software as part of a complete copy of the Qualor
   repository (a fork, with or without your published patches) or of a Qualor release or image
   as published by its maintainers (a mirror). Redistributing it this way gives nobody the right
   to use it in production without a subscription. You may not otherwise distribute, sublicense
   or sell the Software or modified versions of it.

7. Third-party components keep their own licences.

8. THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED "AS IS", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR IMPLIED, INCLUDING
   BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY, FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE AND
   NONINFRINGEMENT. IN NO EVENT SHALL THE AUTHORS OR COPYRIGHT HOLDERS BE LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM,
   DAMAGES OR OTHER LIABILITY, WHETHER IN AN ACTION OF CONTRACT, TORT OR OTHERWISE, ARISING FROM,
